WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.280
This video’s sponsored by Audible.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:09.440
To get a free audiobook, like Game of Thrones
or Dune or Wheel of Time, sign up for a trial

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.992
at the link below.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.840
Game of Thrones author George Martin said
that he likes Tyrion Lannister.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.120
Tyrion is “the villain” of course – but
there’s nothing like a good villain.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.800
The first few seasons of the Thrones TV show
are a.. pretty close adaptation of the books

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.920
– Tyrion is a smart, funny dwarf who uses
his wits in politics, but feels rejected and

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.880
unloved.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.200
When he’s condemned for a crime that he
didn’t commit, he kills his father Tywin

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.560
and his lover Shae.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:47.120
But after Season 4, Tyrion in the show becomes
a totally different character to Tyrion in

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.160
the books.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.960
In the show, Tyrion joins Daenerys cause he
believes she will make the world better.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.920
He tries to help her take the Throne without
killing innocent people, and without killing

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.080
his siblings Cersei and Jaime.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.800
But Tyrion’s plans all fail.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.000
His peace in Meereen fails, his war plans
fail, his Cersei deal fails [including his

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.360
ludicrous wight hunt idea], and his plan
for King’s Landing fails when Daenerys burns

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:11.860
the city.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:18.560
Tyrion used to be a smart and ruthless political
player, but he spends most of the last two

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.120
seasons just standing around looking sad and
helpless.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:29.680
In the finale he tells Jon to kill Dany, and
he says Bran should be king, and everything’s

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.080
sort of okay in the end.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:38.320
Tyrion’s story was about his use of political
power, and his need for love and family.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.000
But the ending of the show doesn’t resolve
these themes.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.360
He fails politically but.. still gets power.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.200
And his family dies and no one loves him,
but he’s.. just kind of okay still.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:57.120
He doesn’t change or grow as a character,
and he barely impacts the story apart from

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.960
the thirty minutes.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.720
The final line of dialogue in Game of Thrones
is Tyrion telling a joke, but we don’t hear

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.760
the punchline.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.520
Which is a good metaphor for Tyrion’s story
in the show – there’s a great set-up in

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.040
the first few seasons, but there’s no punchline,
no emotional payoff in the end.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.640
Because Tyrion in the show is not the real
Tyrion Lannister.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.120
In the books, his story is very different,
and much darker.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.040
After killing Tywin and&nbsp;
Shae, Tyrion is traumatised,&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.480
and angry.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.920
He doesn’t want to protect Cersei and Jaime,
he wants to kill his siblings, for revenge.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.800
And he doesn’t want to protect innocent
people – he wants to bring “fire and sword”

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.080
to Westeros.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.520
He thinks of himself as a “vengeful ghost”
coming to “haunt the Seven Kingdoms” – “They

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.040
would not love me living, so let them dread
me dead”.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.280
So what is Tyrion’s story in the books,
and.. is Tyrion Lannister a villain?

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.280
Tyrion in the books looks very different to
Peter Dinklage in the show.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:09.520
Book-Tyrion is ugly – he has a “brutish”
“squashed-in face”, he’s described as

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.160
“grotesque” “like a gargoyle”.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:18.240
His hair is pale blond, and his eyes are two
different colours – one green and one black.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.920
When Tyrion is wounded in battle, he doesn’t
just get a cool scar – half his nose is

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.440
cut off, leaving his face hideously “disfigured”.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.280
Tyrion’s ugliness is important because it’s
part of why people reject him and see him

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.240
as a monster.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.120
One of the inspirations behind Tyrion’s
character is Richard the Third, who was a

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.440
King of England in the Wars of the Roses.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:46.640
In histories and literature, Richard was portrayed
as a devious villain who killed his family

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.000
to gain power.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.720
And supposedly, Richard was ugly and deformed
with a hunchback – his evil soul was reflected

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.640
in an ugly twisted body.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.280
Modern historians doubt whether any of that
was actually true about Richard.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.280
But the point is that because of Tyrion’s&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.720
ugly appearance, people&nbsp;
are prejudiced against him.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.160
Tyrion was rejected from the day he was born.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.440
Tyrion’s father Tywin was always proud and
ambitious.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:22.480
But Tywin’s father Lord Tytos was weak – his
lords mocked and laughed at him to his face.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:28.080
Young Tywin hated the humiliation and shame
that this brought to their noble family.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.560
So Tywin fought “to restore the pride and
power” of House Lannister, brutally exterminating

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.040
whole families who rebelled against them.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.840
Tywin became Lord of Casterly Rock, and Hand
of the King for Aerys Targaryen.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.680
Tywin married his cousin Joanna, and he loved
her deeply – it’s said that only she saw

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.440
the real Tywin beneath his cold harsh armour.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:58.080
They had twins, Cersei and Jaime – Tywin
wanted Cersei to be queen, and Jaime a great

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.040
knight – he dreamed they’d be “so strong
and brave and beautiful that no one would

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.800
ever laugh at them”.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:10.880
After the humiliation of his father Tytos,
laughter was what Tywin hated most.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:17.680
But then, Joanna died giving birth to Tyrion
– an ugly “malformed” dwarf.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.045
In the superstitious society of Westeros,
people thought Tyrion’s birth was a dark

00:05:18.045 --> 00:05:18.160
omen foretelling disaster.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:23.600
King Aerys mocked Tywin, and said Tyrion was
a punishment from the gods – that they took

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.640
Tywin’s beautiful wife and gave him a monster
to teach him humility.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.240
The smallfolk called Tyrion “Lord Tywin’s
Doom”.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:39.440
So Tyrion’s birth hurt the two things Tywin
loved most – it undermined the pride and

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.560
dignity of House Lannister, and caused the
death of his beloved wife.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.680
So Tywin always hated Tyrion, and was cold
and cruel to him.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.120
Cersei copied her father and also hated Tyrion.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:59.120
The only immediate family who showed Tyrion
any affection or respect was his brother Jaime.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.720
Jaime gave him toys, and taught him to ride
a pony, and Tyrion loved and trusted Jaime

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.320
more than anyone.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.520
He also liked his uncles Tygett and Gerion.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:14.080
Gerion taught Tyrion about the wonders of
the world, and taught him acrobatics, like

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.840
flips and walking on his hands.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:23.520
But Tywin hated Tyrion acting a fool, and
being laughed at, so he stopped the acrobatics.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.720
Tywin also refused to let Tyrion travel the
world with Gerion, and instead put him in

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.840
charge of the drains and cisterns at Casterly
Rock.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:39.200
So Tyrion had a lonely childhood, finding
comfort in books about history and dragons.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:45.040
Rejected by his father and his sister, and
with no mother, Tyrion desperately wanted

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:45.920
to be loved.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.560
When Tyrion was thirteen, he met a common
girl called Tysha.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.200
They fell in love, and got married, happily
living as husband and wife for two weeks.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:01.840
But when Tywin found out, he was furious that
Tyrion had shamed House Lannister by marrying

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.200
an unworthy woman.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:09.600
Jaime told Tyrion that Tysha was a “whore”
– that Jaime paid Tysha to be with Tyrion,

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.600
and that she didn’t really love him.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:16.640
To teach Tyrion a lesson, Tywin had Tysha
raped by his guards.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.400
Then he made Tyrion rape Tysha.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.080
And the marriage was ended.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:28.720
So the one time that Tyrion fell in love with
someone, he learned that that love wasn’t

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:29.440
real.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.520
He was betrayed, humiliated, and forced to
violate and dehumanise his wife.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:42.080
Ever since Tysha, Tyrion believed that no
woman would ever truly love him, that they’d

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.080
only want him for his gold.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.760
So Tyrion turns to sex workers and wine.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:52.960
But Tyrion says that while whores will fuck
you, they won’t kiss you – Tyrion craves

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:56.640
real intimacy, and approval, and a place in
the world.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.720
He’s not a warrior like Jaime.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.720
He doesn’t have power like Tywin.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.960
He’s not feared or loved.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.640
But he is smart.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.600
He’s good at strategy, and manipulating
people.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:13.920
So Tyrion reads lots of books – he says
his mind is his weapon, and his wits are all

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:14.420
he has.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.720
When Tyrion is about 25 years old, Book 1

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.600
begins.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:23.840
He goes up to Winterfell with King Robert
and the rest, and he makes friends with Jon

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:24.340
Snow.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:30.320
In the books, Tyrion does an acrobatic jump
and somersault here, which author George Martin

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.920
later said he.. “could have left out”
cause it’s.. kinda silly.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:39.440
But Jon feels rejected from his family for
being a bastard, just like Tyrion feels rejected

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:40.720
for being a dwarf.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:46.560
So he gives Jon advice – he says when people
make fun of you and call you names, you should

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.760
take that name, and make it your armour.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:55.920
So like when people mock Tyrion and call him
the Imp, Tyrion takes on the persona of a

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.160
sarcastic cynical Imp.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:03.760
He uses jokes and irony as a shield to deflect
the hurt of rejection.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:07.840
And he uses his sharp tongue to make fun of
people back.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.800
Tyrion slaps Joffrey for being a dick.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.480
He stands up for Jon against the bullying
Alliser Thorne, and defeats him in a mighty

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.080
duel with a crab fork.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:24.960
Tyrion gives Bran a special saddle design,
so he can ride a horse after his injury – Tyrion

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:32.240
has sympathy for cripples, bastards and broken
things, he identifies with outcasts and underdogs.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:36.320
But Tyrion can also be cruel and vindictive.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.080
Even in small ways.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:43.760
Like, he dislikes Benjen Stark, so Tyrion
takes Benjen’s warm clothes to make Benjen

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.160
cold, just out of petty spite.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.120
When Catelyn captures Tyrion, he plots revenge
on all her men.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.960
He especially hates the singer Marillion for
making fun of him.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.160
So when they’re attacked, Tyrion stomps
on Marillion’s hand, and breaks his fingers

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.560
– just cause he’s annoyed by this guy’s
singing!

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.400
Lysa falsely accuses Tyrion of murder.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:11.920
And it’s easy to frame Tyrion, because he’s
an ugly Imp, and people are biased against

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:12.560
him.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:18.320
But Tyrion escapes using his wits and his
words – he convinces Bronn, and the mountain

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.000
clansmen to join him.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.680
Tyrion says he’ll help the mountain clansmen
attack the Vale.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.400
And in the books, he’s serious about this.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.360
He plans “to reduce the Vale of Arryn to
a smoking wasteland”.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:36.720
He thinks there’s nothing he’d enjoy more
than getting revenge on Lysa, “except perhaps

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.080
strangling Cersei”.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.800
He often fantasises about killing Cersei and
Tywin.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.840
Even as a child, he dreamed of burning his
sister and father in dragonfire.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:54.640
So from the beginning, book--Tyrion has a
dark side that wasn’t in the TV show.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:11:01.040
Being mistreated and disrespected makes him
angry, and he wants to pay his debts with

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.400
violent revenge.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:09.360
Tyrion meets with his father Tywin as the
Lannisters go to war with the Starks and Tullys.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:14.240
And Tywin fights this war in the most violent
and destructive way possible.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:19.760
He orders his most brutal soldiers like the
Mountain to burn and plunder the riverlands,

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.400
killing and raping innocent people.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.800
And Tyrion doesn’t question this.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.120
He’s there when Tywin gives the orders.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:32.560
He sees villages burned, and sees innocent
people killed by his family.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:37.360
And Tyrion has no sympathy – because Tyrion
thinks like Tywin.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:43.760
It was Tywin who taught Tyrion that a Lannister
pays his debts with brutal indiscriminate

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.400
violence – “I see you have taken a few
lessons from me” Tywin says.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:54.240
And that’s why Tyrion wants violent revenge
on Marillion, the Vale, and ironically, on

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:55.200
Tywin.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:12:01.120
Tyrion does hate Tywin, but he’s still desperate
for his father’s love and approval, so he’s

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.360
internalised Tywin’s brutal methods, and
tries to be like him.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:11.280
But no matter how hard Tyrion tries, Tywin
just criticises and humiliates Tyrion, saying

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.440
he’s weak and useless.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:19.680
Tywin’s constant negging makes Tyrion feel
insecure, inadequate, and unloved.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:25.920
Tywin orders Tyrion to fight on the front
lines of a battle, and Tyrion realises that

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.640
his father wants to get him killed.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:33.840
So before the battle, Tyrion feels lonely,
and he meets a girl called Shae, who agrees

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.480
to be his lover, in return for gold.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:40.000
Shae is just eighteen years old in the books.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:45.360
She’s witty and charming, and when they
have sex, she acts like she enjoys it and

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.680
calls him her “giant of Lannister”.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.680
Tyrion knows she’s just pretending to like
him, but he’s so desperate for love that

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.600
he wants to believe that it’s real.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.160
In the TV show, Shae eventually does love
Tyrion for real.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.000
But not in the books.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:07.040
Author George Martin says Shae doesn’t give
a shit about Tyrion, and is only in it for

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.720
the money and status.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:15.040
And Tyrion knows this, but after his experience
with Tysha, he feels that fake love is all

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:15.680
he can get.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:21.600
At the battle, in the TV show, Tyrion gets
knocked out and misses the whole thing – because

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:25.200
the showrunners didn’t have the budget for
a battle in Season 1.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.480
But in the books, Tyrion rides in and fights
– he kills some blokes, and stabs a horse

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.600
with his hat, and he survives this battle.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:37.040
So [now that Jaime has been captured] Tywin
gives Tyrion a hint of praise and respect

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:37.840
for once.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:42.160
He tells Tyrion to go to King’s Landing
and rule as Hand of the King.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:46.320
But Tywin also tells Tyrion not to bring his
“whore” Shae.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:52.960
The talk of whores brings up Tyrion’s anger
and pain for what Tywin did to Tysha.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:57.040
So Tyrion defies his father and brings Shae
to King’s Landing.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:03.280
So in Book 1, Tyrion is hurt and angry at
world that rejects him.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:06.480
He wants love, and respect, and revenge.

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:10.160
In Book 2, Tyrion takes power in King’s

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.440
Landing, and he says he’s going to do “justice”.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:17.520
He gets rid of the corrupt [gold cloak commander]
Janos Slynt, because Janos’ men killed a

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.040
baby and her mother.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.120
Tyrion imprisons and humiliates Pycelle for
disobeying him.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:28.320
Tyrion blackmails Lancel Lannister, and bribes
the Kettleblacks to spy on Cersei.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:34.160
He sends Myrcella to marry a Martell, and
makes a plan to free Jaime from the Starks.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:40.400
Tyrion feels very impressed with himself for
his clever political plots – he thinks he

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.800
“can scheme with any man”, that this is
what he was made for.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.560
But he’s not really as successful he thinks.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:54.960
Like sure, Tyrion outsmarts Janos and Pycelle
and Lancel, but those guys are small fry – the

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:59.760
real dangerous players are Littlefinger and
Varys, and Tyrion never figures out what they’re

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:00.560
up to.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.200
And many of Tyrion’s plots fail.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:07.360
The Kettleblacks were working for Littlefinger
all along, not Tyrion.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:11.840
Myrcella’s marriage just lets the Martells
use her against the Lannisters.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.480
Tyrion’s plot to free Jaime fails.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.520
And Tyrion’s insults to Pycelle, and Joffrey
and Cersei and the Kingsguard and others just

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.960
create enemies who turn against Tyrion in
the end.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:26.800
So Tyrion is not as clever as he thinks he
is.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.360
And he doesn’t really do justice.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:34.160
Like, sure, he gets rid of Janos Slynt, or
just makes him Jon Snow’s problem, but the

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.440
person who ordered Janos to kill a baby was
Cersei, and Tyrion feels he can’t bring

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:40.400
her to justice.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:46.880
Tyrion also realises that his own men, like
Bronn, are just as cutthroat and immoral as

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.000
Janos was.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.600
So he admits to himself that he isn’t really
doing justice.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:58.800
Ultimately, Tyrion works as Hand of the King
for King Joffrey, a cruel incompetent child

00:15:58.800 --> 00:15:59.600
tyrant.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:02.480
Tyrion knows that Joffrey is a terrible king.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:07.280
And he knows that he isn’t the rightful
king – he’s a bastard of incest, making

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.880
Stannis the true king.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:13.120
Tyrion knows that Cersei and Tywin are cruel
terrible rulers.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:17.760
And he knows that their army commits evil
atrocities in the riverlands.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:23.600
A river lord says that Lannister soldiers
are burning, raping and killing innocent people.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:27.200
And Tyrion doesn’t care, he says that’s
just war.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.520
Which is a bullshit excuse.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:34.240
The Starks and Tullys and Stannis don’t
wage war like that – the Lannisters are

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.080
exceptionally brutal.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:41.280
In between Tyrion’s chapters, we get chapters
from Arya’s perspective, as she experiences

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:47.040
the horror of Lannister atrocities – making
it really clear that Tyrion is on the wrong

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.720
side of this war.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:55.040
All his clever political plots support a brutal
illegitimate government, fighting against

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.080
the heroic Starks and righteous Stannis.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:03.280
Tyrion also mostly ignores the threat of the
white walker apocalypse, even though the Night’s

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:05.120
Watch repeatedly asks him for help.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:09.200
Tyrion doesn’t do justice in Book 2.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.880
It’s not about the realm.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.440
It’s about his ego.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:20.800
After a lifetime of being mocked and disrespected,
Tyrion loves having power and status.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:26.640
He thinks “me, the dwarf, the monster, the
one they scorned and laughed at”, “now

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:32.080
I hold it all, the power, the city, the girl”,
and “I do love it”.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:38.160
Tyrion’s humiliation of Lancel and Pycelle
isn’t about political strategy.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:42.640
It’s about making himself feel powerful,
making himself feel tall.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.520
Tyrion’s feelings of resentment are understandable
and sympathetic.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:54.560
But he uses his power to bully and humiliate,
to feed his ego, and to fight on the wrong

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:56.080
side of this war.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:59.840
That’s why Tyrion is “the villain” in
Book 2.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.720
Throughout the book, Tyrion struggles for
power with Cersei.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.320
They’re both on team Lannister.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.200
But they each want the power for themselves.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.920
So they undermine and lie and insult and spy
on each other.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:20.960
There is one moment when Tyrion and Cersei
celebrate and are happy together, but Tyrion

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:26.880
uses this opportunity to slip Cersei a mild
poison, to get rid of her for a few days.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:32.320
And the relationship really breaks down when
Tyrion gets between Cersei and her children.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.400
Tyrion sends Myrcella to Dorne.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:37.120
He takes Tommen away for safekeeping.

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.960
And he puts Joffrey in a battle.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:44.560
Cersei feels that her children are threatened,
so she retaliates by threatening the people

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.840
Tyrion loves.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:50.880
She captures a sex worker called Alayaya,
thinking that she’s Tyrion’s lover Shae.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.680
And she threatens to torture and kill the
girl if Cersei’s children are hurt.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:58.080
So how does Tyrion react?

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:03.200
He could just tell Cersei the truth – that
she’s got the wrong girl, that Tyrion would

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:08.000
never hurt her children, that they’re on
the same side and shouldn’t fight – but

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:14.480
instead, Tyrion decides to be like Tywin,
and to speak with “his father’s voice”.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:21.840
Tyrion says if Alayaya is beaten and raped,
Tyrion will beat and rape Tommen.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:27.120
He promises to hurt Cersei, to turn her joy
to ashes in her mouth.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:32.080
This is the moment Tyrion and Cersei become
enemies.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:39.200
And it happens because instead of being honest
decent people, they both act like their brutal

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.400
ruthless father.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:47.760
Their petty sibling rivalry for Tywin’s
love spirals into murder, hate, and eventual

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:49.680
disaster for their family.

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:54.160
Tyrion defends King’s Landing from Stannis.

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:59.280
He blows up Stannis’ ships with wildfire,
and in the books he traps the burning ships

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.560
with a giant chain.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:07.200
We see from Davos’ perspective as Tyrion’s
wildfire kills his sons, and thousands of

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:12.480
others – so from Davos’ perspective, Tyrion
is totally the villain.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:17.680
Tyrion leads an attack, and fights amidst
fiery ships like a badass.

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:19.680
But then Tyrion’s attacked by one of

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:26.480
his own men – Mandon Moore slashes Tyrion’s
face open – possibly under Cersei’s orders,

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:29.120
or Joffrey’s, or Littlefinger’s.

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:34.640
But Tyrion goes down, and Tywin and the Tyrells
arrive to win the battle.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:41.200
At the end of the book, Tyrion is badly wounded,
his face is disfigured, and he’s alone.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:48.400
He has fever dreams and visions of the thousands
of people he killed in battle, burned corpses

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.160
weeping and moaning.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.320
He thinks “Why did I kill them all?”

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:58.320
And then he dreams the answer – he dreams
of a feast where everyone praises him as a

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:06.320
hero, Jaime makes him a knight, Shae embraces
him – and his father Tywin smiles with “approval”.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:12.160
This is why Tyrion fought this war, and played
politics.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.640
It’s because he wants to be loved.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.040
But in Book 3, Tyrion gets no love.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:24.560
Tywin takes all the credit for winning the
battle, and takes Tyrion’s power as Hand

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.600
of the King.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:30.960
Tyrion’s allies are replaced and scattered,
and Tyrion feels abandoned.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:36.160
So Tyrion goes to his father and asks for
some “gratitude” and recognition for saving

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:38.800
the city, and bleeding for their family.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:44.880
He asks to be publicly acknowledged as Tywin’s
son and heir – since Jaime is a Kingsguard,

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:48.080
Tyrion should be the next Lord of Casterly
Rock.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:50.160
But Tywin refuses.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:56.080
He calls Tyrion an ill-made “creature”,
“devious”, “spiteful” and full of

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:56.880
lust.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:02.320
He says he’ll never let Tyrion turn Casterly
Rock into his “whorehouse”.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:07.840
Tywin is angry that Tyrion threatened Cersei
to protect Alayaya.

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:12.880
So Tywin has Alayaya whipped, and kicked out
the city gates naked.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:18.800
Tywin brings up Tysha, and Shae, and says
he’ll kill Tyrion’s whores.

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:26.160
So Tywin’s hatred of Tyrion is connected
to Tywin’s feelings about women and sex,

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:30.240
which goes back to Tywin’s relationship
with his own father, Tytos.

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:36.080
Cause after Tywin’s mother died, Tytos took
common women as his mistresses.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:41.520
One mistress became proud and influential,
ordering people around at the Rock.

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:45.280
And she wore Tywin’s mother’s clothes
and jewellery.

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:52.240
Tywin was furious that a lowborn woman had
power and status in House Lannister, and had

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:53.840
impinged on the memory of his mother.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:23:00.800
So when Tytos died, Tywin stripped the woman,
and walked her naked through the streets to

00:23:00.800 --> 00:23:02.960
show the world she was a “whore”.

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:09.120
Now, Tywin does the same thing with Alayaya,
and did something similar with Tysha.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.800
So because of his own daddy issues, Tywin
is paranoid and insecure about lower-class

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:24.000
women undermining his pride, so he uses brutal
sexual violence and public humiliation to

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:27.760
put women beneath the dignity of his noble
house.

00:23:28.816 --> 00:23:34.960
So Tywin hates that Tyrion openly has sex
with lowborn women like Tytos did.

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:39.600
He hates that Tyrion is mocked and laughed
at, like Tytos was.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:43.520
Tywin says “I was made to suffer my father’s
follies.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.280
I will not suffer yours”.

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:49.440
Tyrion reminds Tywin of all&nbsp;
his deepest insecurities&nbsp;

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:52.000
about his father and women and his grief for

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:52.560
his wife.

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:59.760
And it’s not fair, or rational, but that’s
why Tywin hates Tyrion, and rejects him so

00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:00.400
brutally.

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:06.880
Tyrion knows that Shae is in danger from Tywin,
and it’d be safer to send her away.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:10.560
But she’s the only person who makes him
feel loved.

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:13.760
Even though he knows she’s just using him
for his money.

00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:17.360
Shae is not a nice person in the books.

00:24:17.360 --> 00:24:22.320
She says cruel things about Lollys, a disabled
rape victim.

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:25.280
And Tyrion isn’t nice to Shae sometimes.

00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:32.080
He slaps her, he isolates and controls her,
he risks the life of this teenage girl for

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:33.760
his gratification.

00:24:33.760 --> 00:24:36.880
And then Tyrion gets in&nbsp;
another shitty relationship&nbsp;

00:24:36.880 --> 00:24:37.760
with a teenager.

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:44.000
Tywin tells Tyrion to marry Sansa Stark, so
that the Lannisters can use her claim to take

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.200
over the north.

00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:48.320
And Tyrion has mixed feelings.

00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:53.360
He says Sansa is “too young” to marry
– cause she’s just twelve years old in

00:24:53.360 --> 00:24:59.040
the books – but Tyrion would like to rule
Winterfell, and get away from his family.

00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:04.480
Tyrion offers for Sansa to marry Lancel instead,
but Sansa remembers that Tyrion was kind to

00:25:04.480 --> 00:25:10.720
her once, and she hasn’t really got a choice,
so they go along with the wedding.

00:25:10.720 --> 00:25:15.840
Sansa refuses to kneel for the wedding cloak
though, so Tyrion has to stand on the back

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:17.120
of a jester.

00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:21.200
The wedding is humiliating and depressing
for them both.

00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:24.400
Tyrion gets drunk and threatens King Joffrey.

00:25:25.200 --> 00:25:26.480
Then they go to bed.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:33.200
Tywin told Tyrion to have sex with Sansa to
consummate the marriage and secure her claim

00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:34.080
on the north.

00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:37.520
And at first, Tyrion intends to have sex with
her.

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:44.560
But Sansa doesn’t want him, so he relents,
and they settle into their distant uncomfortable

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:45.060
marriage.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:51.120
Tyrion tries to connect with her – he’s
so desperate for love and validation, but

00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:56.240
she doesn’t want him, cause she’s twelve,
and she’s a political prisoner, and Tyrion’s

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:58.160
family killed her family.

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:01.600
So their marriage is “a daily agony”.

00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:06.400
Tywin keeps telling Tyrion to have sex with
Sansa, and Tyrion’s angry that his father

00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:08.880
keeps trying to control his sex life.

00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:14.080
A singer blackmails Tyrion, so Tyrion has
him killed and made into soup.

00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:20.160
Tyrion’s stressed – he has a shitty job
as master of coin, there’re Martells and

00:26:20.160 --> 00:26:21.600
Tyrells to deal with.

00:26:21.600 --> 00:26:27.360
His child wife hates him, his dad wants to
kill his girlfriend, the queen hates him,

00:26:27.360 --> 00:26:32.000
the king hates him, the common people hate
him and think he’s “a twisted little monkey

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:32.500
demon”.

00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:39.280
House Lannister is more powerful than ever,
but Tyrion feels miserable and alone.

00:26:40.240 --> 00:26:45.840
At Joffrey’s wedding, there’s a performance
by some dwarfs, who ride a dog and a pig and

00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:47.680
joust for entertainment.

00:26:47.680 --> 00:26:53.920
Joffrey tells Tyrion to ride the pig, and
Tyrion refuses, so they get angry and insult

00:26:53.920 --> 00:26:55.040
each other publicly.

00:26:55.600 --> 00:27:01.040
Then Joffrey dies of poisoned wine, and Cersei
accuses Tyrion of the murder.

00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:08.880
At the trial, Tyrion has no friends to defend
him – Bronn gets bribed by Cersei, and Podrick

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:10.320
is just a boy.

00:27:10.320 --> 00:27:13.920
What Tyrion does have is a lot of enemies.

00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:19.600
All the people Tyrion threatened and humiliated
over the last two books come back to condemn

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:20.100
him.

00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:26.000
And they make a strong case that Tyrion poisoned
Joffrey, because Tyrion did steal poison,

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:31.120
and he did threaten Joffrey – he publicly
swore to geld Joffrey.

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:36.480
Of course, Tyrion didn’t really intend to
cut off his nephew’s penis.

00:27:36.480 --> 00:27:39.280
Just like he didn’t really want to hurt
Tommen.

00:27:39.280 --> 00:27:44.160
He only made these threats because he was
angry and hurt, and cause he thought that

00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:50.160
acting like Tywin, and playing the role of
a monster would protect him, like armour.

00:27:50.800 --> 00:27:53.280
But it doesn’t work.

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:58.000
Tyrion says he’s been “on trial for being
a dwarf” all his life.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:02.720
And it’s true that people are horribly prejudiced
against him for the way he looks.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:08.720
But it’s also true that Tyrion’s villainous
behaviour – his threats manipulation and

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:12.240
lies – are part of why people treat him
like a villain.

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:19.040
Finally, Shae testifies against Tyrion, after
being bribed and pressured by Cersei.

00:28:19.040 --> 00:28:24.720
Shae says Tyrion is guilty, and humiliates
him by talking about their sex life.

00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:30.320
This betrayal breaks Tyrion, and all his hatred
pours out.

00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:35.840
He says he wants to poison everyone, that
he wishes he was the monster they think he

00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:36.340
is.

00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:43.360
Tyrion demands trial by combat, but the Mountain
kills Oberyn, so Tywin condemns his son to

00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:45.760
death for a crime he didn’t commit.

00:28:46.640 --> 00:28:50.400
Before his execution, Tyrion is saved by Jaime.

00:28:50.400 --> 00:28:56.320
And this is the moment when Tyrion in the
show and Tyrion in the books go in completely

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:57.760
different directions.

00:28:57.760 --> 00:29:03.520
Cause in the show, Tyrion thanks Jaime, and
they hug lovingly, then Tyrion leaves.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:07.360
But in the books, Jaime&nbsp;
makes a terrible revelation.

00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:14.160
After Tyrion married Tysha, Jaime had told
him that Tysha was a whore – that Jaime

00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:17.840
paid her to be with Tyrion, and she didn’t
really love him.

00:29:17.840 --> 00:29:22.240
But now Jaime reveals that that was a lie
that Tywin made him tell.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:30.160
Jaime didn’t pay Tysha, she was just a random
peasant girl who really did love Tyrion.

00:29:31.040 --> 00:29:35.200
All these years, Tyrion thought that no woman
would ever love him.

00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:41.280
But now he finds out that his wife, who was
gang-raped by Tywin’s men, and by Tyrion,

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:44.400
was the only woman who ever loved him.

00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:50.480
Tyrion is devastated, and furious that Jaime
kept to this lie.

00:29:50.480 --> 00:29:54.720
It feels like the ultimate betrayal from the
one person Tyrion thought he could trust.

00:29:55.360 --> 00:30:02.480
All Tyrion’s pain becomes rage, and he swears
to get revenge on his family, to punish the

00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:09.280
world by becoming the villain they think he
is – he says “I am the monster they all

00:30:09.280 --> 00:30:10.000
say I am”.

00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:16.400
Just to hurt Jaime, he says he did kill Joffrey,
and tells him that Cersei’s been cheating

00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:16.900
on him.

00:30:17.360 --> 00:30:25.760
So Tyrion leaves Jaime not as a loving brother,
but as his enemy, a monster wanting revenge.

00:30:25.760 --> 00:30:31.600
And it’s because of the revelation about
Tysha that Tyrion goes after Tywin.

00:30:31.600 --> 00:30:35.840
And in Tywin’s bed, Tyrion finds Shae.

00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:41.600
Tywin had always criticised Tyrion for having
sex with “whores”.

00:30:41.600 --> 00:30:45.840
He says it’s a weakness, and a shame on
their family.

00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:53.120
After Tywin’s wife died, he supposedly never
touched a woman – he “had no use for whores”.

00:30:53.120 --> 00:30:58.800
Tywin acted like he had no lust, no emotions,
just cold rationality.

00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:01.840
But now Tyrion sees that’s a lie.

00:31:02.400 --> 00:31:06.640
Tywin does have sex, just like Tyrion.

00:31:06.640 --> 00:31:08.640
And it’s not just Shae.

00:31:08.640 --> 00:31:13.040
In Book 2, Tyrion uses a secret tunnel that
runs into a brothel.

00:31:13.040 --> 00:31:18.000
Varys says that this tunnel was built for
a Hand of the King so he could visit the brothel

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:18.960
secretly.

00:31:18.960 --> 00:31:25.040
And inside the brothel is a “red and yellow”
window, and “a globe of gilded metal and

00:31:25.040 --> 00:31:28.560
scarlet glass” – those are Lannister colours,
red and gold.

00:31:28.560 --> 00:31:31.200
And Tywin Lannister was Hand of the King.

00:31:31.200 --> 00:31:36.400
So it was probably Tywin who built this tunnel
to visit the brothel on the regular.

00:31:36.400 --> 00:31:42.720
Tywin even lets Shae wear his jewellery, just
like his father’s mistress wore his mother’s

00:31:42.720 --> 00:31:43.220
jewellery.

00:31:43.760 --> 00:31:50.720
So there are some deep dark complicated feelings
about sex and family and shame happening in

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:51.520
Tywin.

00:31:51.520 --> 00:31:57.200
But the point is that Tyrion discovers that
Tywin is a massive hypocrite who does have

00:31:57.200 --> 00:32:00.080
sex with “whores” just like he does.

00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:07.040
In the show, when Tyrion finds Shae, Shae
grabs a knife, and they struggle, before Tyrion

00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:08.160
kills her.

00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:12.640
Then he cries, and apologises to her corpse.

00:32:12.640 --> 00:32:17.840
The show tries to make the scene feel tragic,
almost sympathetic to Tyrion.

00:32:17.840 --> 00:32:21.360
But in the books, it’s cold-blooded murder.

00:32:21.360 --> 00:32:23.520
Shae doesn’t grab a knife.

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:30.160
Shae cries, and says she didn’t want to
betray Tyrion, that Cersei made her, and Tywin

00:32:30.160 --> 00:32:30.960
scares her.

00:32:31.520 --> 00:32:39.120
But Tyrion is angry at her betrayal, so he
strangles her to death without mercy.

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:45.680
Compared to the show, this is a much more
brutal, evil murder – author George Martin

00:32:45.680 --> 00:32:50.560
calls it his “blackest deed”, “the great
crime of his soul”.

00:32:51.440 --> 00:32:57.040
Then Tyrion gets a crossbow and finds his
noble father on the toilet.

00:32:57.040 --> 00:33:02.400
He asks Tywin what happened to Tysha – where
did she go after the gang-rape?

00:33:02.960 --> 00:33:08.960
Tywin doesn’t know and doesn’t care, he
says Tysha went “Wherever whores go”.

00:33:09.520 --> 00:33:11.680
So Tyrion shoots his father.

00:33:12.400 --> 00:33:18.960
Tywin says Tyrion is “no son of mine”,
but Tyrion says “I’m you writ small”

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:21.360
– meaning ‘I’m just like you’.

00:33:21.920 --> 00:33:26.960
Cause Tywin hates Tyrion for being devious,
spiteful, and lustful.

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:32.960
But it turns out, Tywin is just as devious
spiteful and lustful as Tyrion.

00:33:32.960 --> 00:33:36.000
Tywin is devious when he plots the Red Wedding.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:41.200
He was spiteful when he killed Elia Martell,
and the Reynes and Castameres.

00:33:41.200 --> 00:33:46.800
And he’s so goddamn lustful that he roots
his son’s girlfriend and builds a secret

00:33:46.800 --> 00:33:48.880
personal sex tunnel to a brothel.

00:33:49.520 --> 00:33:55.760
Tywin and Tyrion have the same insecurities
about being laughed at and feeling weak and

00:33:55.760 --> 00:33:56.880
ashamed.

00:33:56.880 --> 00:34:03.040
Tywin tries to hide his feelings behind the
image of a noble rational golden lion, someone

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:08.000
who’s above the petty shameful behaviour
of his dwarf son.

00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:09.520
But it’s a lie.

00:34:09.520 --> 00:34:14.720
It’s all bullshit, and that’s why Tywin
dies shitting himself on the toilet.

00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:18.320
Tywin “did not, in the end, shit gold”.

00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:20.560
Because he’s not a golden lion.

00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:28.640
He is a deeply flawed man full of shame and
spite and lust, just like his son Tyrion.

00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:37.440
In Book 3, Tyrion tries be loved by his family
and Shae and Sansa, but he is betrayed and

00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:40.000
condemned by everyone close to him.

00:34:41.600 --> 00:34:46.720
In Book 5, Tyrion goes east, drinking his
way across the sea.

00:34:46.720 --> 00:34:54.240
He is consumed with self-loathing, anger,
and despair – he’s lost everything.

00:34:54.240 --> 00:35:00.000
He no longer dreams of love or justice – all
he has left is hatred.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:06.400
He wants to kill Jaime and Cersei, and bring
war to Westeros, he wants to punish the world

00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:07.840
for rejecting him.

00:35:07.840 --> 00:35:10.560
And he especially hates women.

00:35:10.560 --> 00:35:16.400
Tyrion threatens a slave, saying he’ll have
sex with her and murder her, just for the

00:35:16.400 --> 00:35:18.800
pleasure of making her afraid.

00:35:19.520 --> 00:35:26.960
Tyrion’s in a very dark place, and he reacts
to his trauma and pain by hurting others and

00:35:26.960 --> 00:35:27.520
himself.

00:35:28.480 --> 00:35:34.960
In Pentos, Tyrion meets Illyrio, who’s working
with Varys to help Daenerys conquer Westeros.

00:35:34.960 --> 00:35:40.080
He convinces Tyrion to join Daenerys, so that
Tyrion can get revenge on the Lannisters,

00:35:40.080 --> 00:35:42.160
and take Casterly Rock for himself.

00:35:42.720 --> 00:35:48.880
So Tyrion travels with a group of Illyrio’s
allies, led by this guy Griff, and this kid

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:49.920
Young Griff.

00:35:49.920 --> 00:35:53.360
There’s also a septa, and a scholar, and
a knight.

00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:57.920
And Tyrion figures out that Griff and his
crew are not who they seem.

00:35:57.920 --> 00:36:02.400
Griff is actually Jon Connington, who was
once a lord in Westeros.

00:36:02.400 --> 00:36:09.120
And Young Griff is actually supposedly Aegon
Targaryen, the son of Prince Rhaegar and Elia

00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:11.840
Martell who everyone thought was dead.

00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:17.760
Griff and Illyrio and Varys have raised Aegon
to be King – they hope to marry him to Daenerys

00:36:17.760 --> 00:36:21.360
so they can conquer and rule Westeros together.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:29.280
So they travel downriver and see some wondrous
sights – there’s a giant turtle, a naked

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.800
nun, and a strange shape in the fog that may
or may not be a dragon.

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:41.440
In the Sorrows, they see the ancient ruins
of the Bridge of Dream and the Palace of Love,

00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:46.960
just like Tyrion’s dreams and loves are
now ruined – which is one of George Martin’s

00:36:46.960 --> 00:36:48.800
less.. subtle metaphors.

00:36:48.800 --> 00:36:54.960
The Sorrows are a strange and spooky place,
said to be ruled by a dark, mystical figure

00:36:54.960 --> 00:36:56.880
called the Shrouded Lord.

00:36:56.880 --> 00:37:02.880
Their boat inexplicably magically goes through
the same place twice(?!), and then they’re

00:37:02.880 --> 00:37:07.680
attacked by stone men – people infected
with greyscale.

00:37:07.680 --> 00:37:14.400
Tyrion saves Aegon, Jon Connington saves Tyrion,
and JonCon gets infected with greyscale, but

00:37:14.400 --> 00:37:20.080
keeps it a secret – in the TV show, Jorah
gets greyscale, but in the books it’s JonCon.

00:37:20.080 --> 00:37:26.000
And the disease makes JonCon desperate to
make Aegon King of Westeros ASAP – because

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:29.920
JonCon was in love with Aegon’s father,
Prince Rhaegar.

00:37:29.920 --> 00:37:35.040
He feels guilty for failing Rhaegar, and wants
to redeem himself by getting Aegon on the

00:37:35.040 --> 00:37:35.920
Throne.

00:37:35.920 --> 00:37:41.520
He and his crew have spent years training
and protecting Aegon in secret, and now it’s

00:37:41.520 --> 00:37:45.040
almost time to reveal him&nbsp;
and claim his birthright.

00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:51.520
But Tyrion.. really doesn’t give a fuck
about JonCon and Aegon’s quest.

00:37:51.520 --> 00:37:58.080
He makes fun of Aegon’s story as a perfect
handsome fantasy prince, and he undermines

00:37:58.080 --> 00:38:03.200
their noble heroism with his sarcasm and cynicism
and hate.

00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:09.360
It’s almost.. meta how Tyrion mocks the
fantasy tropes of the story that he’s in,

00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:13.360
like Rick Sanchez being so&nbsp;
depressed and disillusioned&nbsp;

00:38:13.360 --> 00:38:15.840
and drunk that he breaks the fourth wall a

00:38:15.840 --> 00:38:16.640
little.

00:38:16.640 --> 00:38:23.040
Tyrion even dresses in motley like a jester
– a villainous fool who makes fun of the

00:38:23.040 --> 00:38:26.320
world like an edgy Westerosi Joker.

00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:30.720
Tyrion hates JonCon because he reminds him
of Tywin.

00:38:30.720 --> 00:38:34.320
And Aegon is an annoying hot-headed teenager.

00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:38.560
So Tyrion mischievously messes with their
plans.

00:38:39.200 --> 00:38:45.040
Over a game of cyvasse, which is the Game
of Thrones version of chess, Tyrion manipulates

00:38:45.040 --> 00:38:48.160
Aegon, and convinces him to change his plan.

00:38:48.160 --> 00:38:53.840
Instead of going east and joining forces with
Daenerys, he tells Aegon to go west and attack

00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:55.840
Westeros by himself.

00:38:55.840 --> 00:39:02.080
And since Aegon is young and rash, and JonCon
is impatient with his greyscale, the madlads

00:39:02.080 --> 00:39:03.200
actually do it.

00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:07.280
They abandon the plan, and attack Westeros
without Daenerys.

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:13.120
Tyrion doesn’t actually think this a good
idea – he only suggests it to mess with

00:39:13.120 --> 00:39:15.120
them, and create chaos.

00:39:15.120 --> 00:39:18.960
But this decision could have huge consequences.

00:39:18.960 --> 00:39:25.040
Like, if Aegon takes the Throne himself, he
and Daenerys could become enemies instead

00:39:25.040 --> 00:39:26.160
of allies.

00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:31.760
There are hints that Aegon is not really a
Targaryen, he’s actually a Blackfyre.

00:39:31.760 --> 00:39:36.800
And Daenerys is warned of a “mummer’s
dragon” or false dragon.

00:39:36.800 --> 00:39:42.560
There are hints of a war between them, a “dance
of the dragons” that will cause death and

00:39:42.560 --> 00:39:45.040
destruction across Westeros.

00:39:45.040 --> 00:39:49.680
So Tyrion’s trolling might cause a terrible
war.

00:39:49.680 --> 00:39:51.200
And he doesn’t care.

00:39:51.200 --> 00:39:53.760
He laughs when he finds out.

00:39:53.760 --> 00:39:58.960
In his anger and nihilism, Tyrion wants to
see the world burn.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:05.280
Tyrion is haunted by memories of Tywin, Shae,
and Tysha.

00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:11.520
Since Tysha was the one woman who truly loved
him, he wants to find her again.

00:40:11.520 --> 00:40:15.680
He imagines them living together in their
cottage like they did when they were young

00:40:15.680 --> 00:40:16.800
and happy.

00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:22.240
It’s not a realistic dream, but that distant
memory is all he’s got.

00:40:22.880 --> 00:40:26.720
Tywin said that Tysha went “Wherever whores
go”.

00:40:26.720 --> 00:40:30.320
So Tyrion repeatedly asks “Where do whores
go?”.

00:40:30.960 --> 00:40:33.840
Thinking of Tysha, he visits a brothel.

00:40:33.840 --> 00:40:40.000
And he has sex with a slave prostitute who
has dead eyes and a scarred back.

00:40:40.720 --> 00:40:45.040
Tyrion feels wretched, full of shame and guilt
and self-hatred.

00:40:45.040 --> 00:40:50.640
He drinks til he pukes, tells the slave to
kill him, and then has sex with her again,

00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:54.560
even though she clearly doesn’t want to
– he rapes her.

00:40:55.600 --> 00:41:01.120
But in the TV show version of the scene, Tyrion
is charming and nice.

00:41:01.120 --> 00:41:08.400
A slave offers him free sex, but Tyrion declines
because he’s so sad, in like a noble kind

00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:08.900
of way.

00:41:09.680 --> 00:41:12.080
The show whitewashes Tyrion.

00:41:12.080 --> 00:41:18.000
It takes out the bad stuff he does and makes
him into a generic good guy who doesn’t

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:20.000
change as a character.

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:26.960
But the books go deep into Tyrion’s emotional
devastation, and he does terrible things.

00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:33.680
Tyrion is captured by Jorah, who wants to
give him to Daenerys to get back in her favour.

00:41:33.680 --> 00:41:39.600
And they go to Volantis, an ancient slave
city in a state of political unrest.

00:41:39.600 --> 00:41:44.960
Cause the rulers of Volantis plan to attack
Daenerys because Daenerys is fighting against

00:41:44.960 --> 00:41:45.840
slavery.

00:41:45.840 --> 00:41:50.000
But the slaves of Volantis see Daenerys as
a beacon of freedom.

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:54.320
And the red priests preach that Daenerys is
the prophesied saviour Azor Ahai.

00:41:54.880 --> 00:41:59.600
A woman called the widow of the waterfront
tells Tyrion that the slaves are waiting for

00:41:59.600 --> 00:42:02.320
Daenerys to come and free them.

00:42:02.320 --> 00:42:07.840
Tyrion agrees go help Daenerys – but not
for heroic reasons.

00:42:07.840 --> 00:42:13.680
He says he’ll bring Daenerys his “hate”,
and the only reward he asks is to be allowed

00:42:13.680 --> 00:42:16.720
to rape and kill his sister Cersei.

00:42:17.600 --> 00:42:21.760
Tyrion embraces the role of monstrous villain.

00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:27.680
Over in Braavos, Arya’s in a play where
the Tyrion character says “As I cannot be

00:42:27.680 --> 00:42:33.760
the hero, let me be the monster, and lesson
them in fear in place of love”.

00:42:34.720 --> 00:42:39.440
Then, Tyrion is attacked by a dwarf girl called
Penny.

00:42:39.440 --> 00:42:42.880
Penny was one of the performers back at Joffrey’s
wedding.

00:42:42.880 --> 00:42:47.840
But when Tyrion escaped Westeros, Cersei put
a bounty on Tyrion’s head.

00:42:47.840 --> 00:42:53.760
So a bunch of idiot bounty hunters have killed
innocent dwarfs, thinking they might be Tyrion.

00:42:53.760 --> 00:43:01.040
Penny’s brother Oppo was one of those killed,
and in her grief and anger, Penny blames Tyrion.

00:43:01.760 --> 00:43:06.880
Tyrion takes pity on Penny, and brings her
with them as they sail east.

00:43:06.880 --> 00:43:11.040
Eventually, Tyrion and Penny reconcile, and
become friends.

00:43:11.040 --> 00:43:12.560
They’ve got a lot in common.

00:43:12.560 --> 00:43:16.720
They’re both dwarfs who have lost their
families and their ways of life.

00:43:16.720 --> 00:43:20.960
They’re both dealing with grief, anger,
and suicidal thoughts.

00:43:21.520 --> 00:43:25.920
But unlike Tyrion, Penny moves past her anger.

00:43:25.920 --> 00:43:28.960
She forgives Tyrion for her brother’s death.

00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:36.560
And instead of wallowing in hatred and despair
like Tyrion, Penny is optimistic, with hopes

00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:38.160
and dreams for the future.

00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:43.840
Penny tells Tyrion to stop his self-destructive
behaviour.

00:43:43.840 --> 00:43:48.080
Like, Tyrion makes fun of Jorah until Jorah
hits Tyrion.

00:43:48.080 --> 00:43:52.560
And Penny tells him he’s gotta stop provoking
people or he’ll get himself killed.

00:43:52.560 --> 00:43:57.280
It used to be that Tyrion could say what he
liked, cause he was a rich and powerful nobleman.

00:43:57.280 --> 00:44:03.280
But now as an exile, he’s no one, so when
he talks shit he gets hit.

00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:09.600
Tyrion has always felt sorry for himself,
but he was very lucky to be born into a rich

00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:10.800
noble family.

00:44:10.800 --> 00:44:14.160
He’s been protected by his privilege all
his life.

00:44:14.160 --> 00:44:20.640
But Penny is a common person as well as dwarf,
and she’s learned the hard way how to survive.

00:44:21.600 --> 00:44:27.360
Tyrion hates being laughed at, but Penny says
making people laugh can be a good thing.

00:44:27.360 --> 00:44:33.280
In fact, if Tyrion had ridden her pig at Joffrey’s
wedding like Joffrey asked, instead of insulting

00:44:33.280 --> 00:44:38.480
Joffrey, Tyrion might never have been condemned,
and Penny’s brother might not have died.

00:44:39.200 --> 00:44:41.840
No one should have to put up with humiliation.

00:44:41.840 --> 00:44:45.600
But many of Tyrion’s problems are caused
by his pride.

00:44:46.240 --> 00:44:51.360
When morale on their ship gets dangerously
low, Penny convinces Tyrion to perform a joust

00:44:51.360 --> 00:44:54.080
with her, riding her pig against her dog.

00:44:54.800 --> 00:45:01.680
So Penny challenges Tyrion’s pride, his
privilege, his self-destructive behaviour.

00:45:01.680 --> 00:45:05.920
She shows him that he’s not the only dwarf
in the world who’s suffered.

00:45:05.920 --> 00:45:09.280
And that it’s possible to forgive and hope.

00:45:10.240 --> 00:45:14.000
Penny has a crush on Tyrion, and they kiss
a couple of times.

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:17.120
But Tyrion isn’t interested in her like
that.

00:45:17.120 --> 00:45:21.600
The only woman he loves is his idealised memory
of Tysha.

00:45:21.600 --> 00:45:25.440
So Tyrion has a complicated relationship with
Penny.

00:45:25.440 --> 00:45:32.240
He’s protective of her, and kind, sometimes,
but he rejects her love, and he mostly rejects

00:45:32.240 --> 00:45:34.640
her positive, hopeful attitude.

00:45:34.640 --> 00:45:38.400
Tyrion stays angry and proud and cynical.

00:45:38.400 --> 00:45:40.800
And he moves closer to power.

00:45:41.600 --> 00:45:47.520
A red priest called Moqorro has a vision of
Tyrion with dragons – “Dragons old and

00:45:47.520 --> 00:45:53.520
young, true and false, bright and dark”
– with Tyrion snarling in their midst, a

00:45:53.520 --> 00:45:56.320
small man with a big shadow.

00:45:56.320 --> 00:45:59.200
The old dragons could be Aemon or Bloodraven.

00:45:59.200 --> 00:46:05.520
The young and true dragons could be Daenerys
and Jon Snow who is probably secretly a Targaryen.

00:46:05.520 --> 00:46:10.800
And the false, dark dragon could be Aegon
– cause he might actually be a Blackfyre

00:46:10.800 --> 00:46:12.240
not a Targaryen.

00:46:12.240 --> 00:46:16.480
And through these dragons, Tyrion will have
a big impact on the story.

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:20.960
In Book 1, Tyrion cast a shadow as “tall
as a king”.

00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:26.720
Aemon said Tyrion “is a giant come among
us, here at the end of the world”.

00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:32.240
So there’s lots of foreshadowing that Tyrion
will play a big role in the endgame of the

00:46:32.240 --> 00:46:32.740
story.

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:38.640
Their ship is damaged in a storm, Moqorro
floats off to Victarion, and Tyrion Penny

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:44.000
and Jorah are captured by slavers outside
Meereen – the city is under siege by the

00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:47.360
slavers of Yunkai while Daenerys tries to
negotiate peace.

00:46:48.320 --> 00:46:54.240
Tyrion, Penny and Jorah are bought as slaves
by a Yunkishman called Yezzan zo Qaggaz, or

00:46:54.240 --> 00:46:55.840
the Yellow Whale.

00:46:55.840 --> 00:47:02.080
Yezzan is enormously rich and enormously fat,
and he keeps a grotesquery of slaves with

00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:06.480
unusual bodies, watched over by his cruel
overseer, Nurse.

00:47:07.200 --> 00:47:14.000
Tyrion has gone from a proud powerful ruler
in Westeros to a powerless humiliated slave.

00:47:14.800 --> 00:47:19.600
Inside Meereen, Daenerys tries to make peace
with the slavers by marrying Hizdahr, and

00:47:19.600 --> 00:47:21.280
opening the fighting pits.

00:47:21.280 --> 00:47:26.560
Tyrion and Penny are made to perform for the
crowds – so the first time Tyrion and Daenerys

00:47:26.560 --> 00:47:29.760
see each other, Tyrion is riding a pig.

00:47:29.760 --> 00:47:33.840
Though she doesn’t know he’s Tyrion, and
they still haven’t met.

00:47:33.840 --> 00:47:40.000
Cause Drogon crashes the party, Daenerys flies
off, and Yunkai prepares to attack Meereen.

00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:44.640
A disease called the bloody flux breaks out,
and Yezzan gets sick.

00:47:44.640 --> 00:47:48.720
Yezzan was dying already from an exotic disease
he got in Sothoryos.

00:47:48.720 --> 00:47:53.760
So pretty soon he’s squirting his guts out,
and Tyrion takes the opportunity to escape.

00:47:54.320 --> 00:47:59.440
On the way out, Tyrion kills Nurse with some
poison mushrooms – and says “A Lannister

00:47:59.440 --> 00:48:01.120
always pays his debts”.

00:48:01.760 --> 00:48:07.360
So after all the crazy stuff that happens
in this book, Tyrion is still a Lannister.

00:48:07.360 --> 00:48:12.240
He’s still proud, spiteful, and murderous,
like his father.

00:48:12.240 --> 00:48:17.200
The main way that Tyrion has changed since
the start of Book 5 is that he’s less depressed

00:48:17.200 --> 00:48:19.760
now, he doesn’t want to die any more.

00:48:19.760 --> 00:48:25.280
He originally considered using these poisoned
mushrooms to kill himself in Pentos, but now

00:48:25.280 --> 00:48:28.080
he chooses to live, and get revenge.

00:48:28.960 --> 00:48:34.960
Tyrion goes to a mercenary captain called
Brown Ben Plumm, commander of the Second Sons.

00:48:34.960 --> 00:48:41.280
Tyrion convinces him to let him and Penny
and Jorah join his company to escape slavery.

00:48:41.280 --> 00:48:46.480
And in return, Tyrion promises Ben money and
a lordship when Tyrion gets power back in

00:48:46.480 --> 00:48:47.600
Westeros.

00:48:47.600 --> 00:48:52.560
So Tyrion Penny and Jorah escape slavery,
but now they’re stuck in the middle of a

00:48:52.560 --> 00:48:55.600
battle between the slavers and Daenerys’
forces.

00:48:55.600 --> 00:48:58.960
Daenerys herself is still missing in the Dothraki
Sea.

00:48:58.960 --> 00:49:04.320
So Barristan commands her army, alongside
Grey Worm and the Unsullied, some sellswords,

00:49:04.320 --> 00:49:05.840
and freed slaves.

00:49:05.840 --> 00:49:10.560
Ben Plumm and the Second Sons are on the side
of the slavers, but Tyrion hopes to convince

00:49:10.560 --> 00:49:12.560
them to join Daenerys instead.

00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:18.720
So Tyrion’s back in the game of thrones,
playing politics, being a Lannister again.

00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:25.120
And he is as ruthless as ever – he compares
himself to Tywin, and thinks about poisoning

00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:26.000
wells.

00:49:26.000 --> 00:49:30.640
Tyrion wants to join Daenerys but not because
he.. believes in her or anything.

00:49:30.640 --> 00:49:35.760
He just thinks that she’s his best hope
of bringing fire and sword to Westeros.

00:49:36.320 --> 00:49:42.960
So in Book 5, Tyrion loses everything, and
falls deep into despair and hate.

00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:46.080
But now, he’s returning to the game of thrones.

00:49:46.080 --> 00:49:51.120
When he gets power, will he use it for violence
and vengeance like Tywin would?

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:54.640
Or will he find forgiveness and hope like
Penny?

00:49:55.600 --> 00:50:00.000
Author George Martin has released sample
chapters of the upcoming next book, The Winds

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:00.880
of Winter.

00:50:00.880 --> 00:50:05.200
In the opening chapters, Tyrion convinces
Ben Plumm and his men to switch sides and

00:50:05.200 --> 00:50:06.400
join Daenerys.

00:50:06.400 --> 00:50:10.400
Another sellsword company called the Windblown
also join Daenerys.

00:50:10.400 --> 00:50:14.800
Victarion Greyjoy and Moqorro arrive with
the ironborn and attack the slavers.

00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:17.920
The dragons Rhaegal and Viserion are loose.

00:50:17.920 --> 00:50:20.560
And Ser Barristan rides into battle.

00:50:21.200 --> 00:50:27.280
So it looks like Daenerys’ forces will defeat
the slavers, leaving a very strange bunch

00:50:27.280 --> 00:50:29.360
of characters in charge of Meereen.

00:50:30.080 --> 00:50:35.200
Barristan is Daenerys’ closest ally, so
Tyrion will want to win his trust – though

00:50:35.200 --> 00:50:40.320
Tyrion suspects that Barristan will hate him
for being a villainous kinslayer.

00:50:40.320 --> 00:50:46.080
Victarion wants to marry Daenerys and steal
her dragons, which probably won’t end well

00:50:46.080 --> 00:50:46.640
for him.

00:50:46.640 --> 00:50:51.440
But if he survives the battle, we could get
some fun dialogue with Tyrion making fun of

00:50:51.440 --> 00:50:54.240
Victarion “dumb as a stump” Greyjoy.

00:50:54.240 --> 00:50:58.160
Moqorro could teach Tyrion more about magic
and prophecy.

00:50:58.160 --> 00:51:02.800
Marwyn the Mage should arrive sometime, and
he’s also into magic and books.

00:51:02.800 --> 00:51:08.080
Ben Plumm and the Tattered Prince will want
battle and plunder, Jorah wants to get out

00:51:08.080 --> 00:51:13.440
of the friendzone with Daenerys, though he’s
picked up an unfortunate face tattoo recently.

00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:16.400
Daario is still around, and he wants Daenerys.

00:51:16.400 --> 00:51:19.040
And Strong Belwas wants.. liver and onions.

00:51:19.600 --> 00:51:24.240
It’s a colourful collection of characters,
and a great opportunity for Tyrion to play

00:51:24.240 --> 00:51:30.080
politics, crack jokes, rule Meereen, and set
himself up as an advisor to Daenerys when

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:30.880
she returns.

00:51:31.520 --> 00:51:34.480
Daenerys won’t trust Tyrion right away.

00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:39.600
Cause Tyrion is a Lannister, condemned as
treacherous kingslayer.

00:51:39.600 --> 00:51:43.760
But Tyrion is very good at convincing people
to make alliances.

00:51:43.760 --> 00:51:48.000
And Tyrion has lots of useful information
that Daenerys needs.

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:50.880
Daenerys has never been to mainland Westeros.

00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:53.120
She doesn’t know her enemies.

00:51:53.120 --> 00:51:58.960
But Tyrion intimately knows Cersei, Jaime,
King Tommen, and other lords.

00:51:58.960 --> 00:52:02.800
Tyrion knows the defences of King’s Landing
and Casterly Rock.

00:52:02.800 --> 00:52:08.560
And Tyrion is the only person in Meereen who
knows about Aegon and JonCon.

00:52:08.560 --> 00:52:13.920
Tyrion can tell her that Aegon is on his way
to take her Throne, which could convince Daenerys

00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:16.080
to get to Westeros ASAP.

00:52:16.080 --> 00:52:22.000
Tyrion could manipulate Daenerys and tell
her that that Aegon is her enemy, to encourage

00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:23.440
conflict and chaos.

00:52:24.240 --> 00:52:28.560
So, like in the show, Tyrion will probably
become Daenerys’ advisor or Hand of the

00:52:28.560 --> 00:52:29.280
Queen.

00:52:29.280 --> 00:52:33.840
But his advice to Daenerys may be very different
to the show.

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:38.960
In the show, Tyrion tells Daenerys to be merciful
to the slavers, so instead of killing them

00:52:38.960 --> 00:52:43.280
all, they just kill some and give the rest
a stern talking to.

00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:49.040
But book Tyrion, in his anger and hate, won’t
want mercy for the people who just enslaved

00:52:49.040 --> 00:52:51.360
him – he’ll want revenge.

00:52:51.360 --> 00:52:54.160
Book Daenerys also wants violence.

00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:59.680
All through Book 5, she tries to rule Meereen
peacefully – making compromises, marrying

00:52:59.680 --> 00:53:02.320
Hizdahr, chaining her dragons.

00:53:02.320 --> 00:53:07.920
But peace fails, so she flies off on her dragon,
and she has visions reminding her that she

00:53:07.920 --> 00:53:13.520
is “the blood of the dragon”, that Meereen
is not her home, that the Targaryen words

00:53:13.520 --> 00:53:15.200
are “Fire and Blood”.

00:53:15.760 --> 00:53:20.160
Daenerys is done with peace, she’s set to
burn her enemies.

00:53:20.160 --> 00:53:26.400
And Daenerys once said that if Yunkai attacks
her, she will raze their city to the ground.

00:53:26.400 --> 00:53:31.680
So Daenerys and Tyrion’s first act together
won’t be this half-assed compromise.

00:53:31.680 --> 00:53:34.320
It might be to destroy Yunkai.

00:53:34.960 --> 00:53:40.000
George Martin said Daenerys has “embraced
her heritage as a Targaryen”, and she and

00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:41.840
Tyrion are “coming home”.

00:53:42.640 --> 00:53:46.000
But it’s a long way from Meereen to Westeros.

00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:48.960
And they have unfinished business in Essos.

00:53:48.960 --> 00:53:54.160
The red priests and the widow of the waterfront
want Daenerys to free the slaves of Volantis.

00:53:54.160 --> 00:53:59.520
Which might get violent – a priest prophesies
that Volantis will burn.

00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:04.960
And conveniently, the ruling slavers of Volantis
live within the Black Walls in the heart of

00:54:04.960 --> 00:54:10.880
the city – making them a convenient target
for Daenerys to roast them all with dragonfire.

00:54:10.880 --> 00:54:16.400
Moqorro may convince Daenerys of her destiny
to be “a sword of fire that will cleanse

00:54:16.400 --> 00:54:20.160
the world”, pushing her further towards
violence.

00:54:20.800 --> 00:54:23.440
Daenerys also has business in Pentos.

00:54:23.440 --> 00:54:28.560
Cause the captain of the Windblown, the Tattered
Prince, joins Daenerys on the condition that

00:54:28.560 --> 00:54:30.880
he gets to take over Pentos.

00:54:30.880 --> 00:54:35.360
Daenerys hasn’t agreed to this yet – at
first she says she won’t give Pentos to

00:54:35.360 --> 00:54:39.840
Tatters, because Illyrio lives in Pentos,
and Illyrio is her trusted ally.

00:54:40.400 --> 00:54:46.000
But Tyrion can tell Daenerys the truth – that
Illyrio has been lying and manipulating her

00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:47.120
all along.

00:54:47.120 --> 00:54:52.880
Illyrio really supports Aegon, and while Illyrio
was selling Daenerys to the Dothraki, he was

00:54:52.880 --> 00:54:55.600
raising Aegon in secrecy and safety.

00:54:56.160 --> 00:55:02.400
Tyrion could convince Daenerys to burn Illyrio
for his betrayal, and to give Pentos to the

00:55:02.400 --> 00:55:03.280
Tattered Prince.

00:55:03.840 --> 00:55:08.560
We don’t know what Tatters’ plans are
for Pentos, but it’s probably something

00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:09.280
bad.

00:55:09.280 --> 00:55:14.480
Tatters has history with Pentos, and he’s
a cruel and brutal man.

00:55:14.480 --> 00:55:19.840
One time, Tatters cut off a guy’s foot,
then forced him to eat it, and then made him

00:55:19.840 --> 00:55:22.880
his cook, that’s the sort of guy Tatters
is.

00:55:22.880 --> 00:55:26.720
And Daenerys and Tyrion might give him the
city of Pentos.

00:55:27.360 --> 00:55:33.200
So there are strong hints in the books that
Daenerys’ journey across Essos will be violent

00:55:33.200 --> 00:55:37.040
and destructive, bringing fire and blood across
the continent.

00:55:37.600 --> 00:55:40.240
Will Tyrion encourage this violence?

00:55:40.240 --> 00:55:42.640
Or will he tell Daenerys to be more peaceful?

00:55:43.360 --> 00:55:48.400
Tyrion’s peaceful, compassionate side is
represented by his relationship with Penny.

00:55:48.400 --> 00:55:54.000
And in his latest chapters, he rejects her
optimism pretty harshly – he slaps her,

00:55:54.000 --> 00:55:58.560
tells her to stop dreaming, and to face harsh
reality.

00:55:58.560 --> 00:56:01.920
There are even hints that Tyrion might hurt
Penny.

00:56:01.920 --> 00:56:04.960
Tyrion dreams of shooting Penny with a crossbow.

00:56:04.960 --> 00:56:10.480
And there’s a weird dark moment when Penny
reminds Tyrion of Shae, and he’s overwhelmed

00:56:10.480 --> 00:56:14.000
with rage, and Tyrion thinks about killing
Penny.

00:56:14.640 --> 00:56:21.680
If Tyrion kills Penny, or just rejects or
loses her somehow, that could be the breaking

00:56:21.680 --> 00:56:26.560
point that leads Tyrion to fully embrace Daenerys’
bloody conquest.

00:56:27.600 --> 00:56:32.080
And Tyrion might develop a connection with
Daenerys’ dragons.

00:56:32.080 --> 00:56:37.200
Tyrion has always been fascinated with dragons,
so he’s read lots of books about them.

00:56:37.200 --> 00:56:41.600
This knowledge is considered so valuable that
JonCon makes him write down everything he

00:56:41.600 --> 00:56:44.000
knows about dragons in case it’s useful.

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:47.600
So this knowledge is another way Tyrion can
help Daenerys.

00:56:47.600 --> 00:56:50.240
Cause Daenerys doesn’t actually know much&nbsp;

00:56:50.240 --> 00:56:53.040
about dragons, she has a&nbsp;
lot of trouble controlling

00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:54.000
hers in the books.

00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:57.120
They keep disobeying her, and eating children.

00:56:57.120 --> 00:56:58.400
They didn’t come with a manual.

00:56:58.400 --> 00:56:58.720
[She can’t Google it].

00:56:58.720 --> 00:57:04.560
So Tyrion might help Daenerys control her
dragons, maybe even breed them, or design

00:57:04.560 --> 00:57:09.280
dragon armour, or a dragon-riding saddle,
like the saddle he designed for Bran.

00:57:09.920 --> 00:57:14.160
And maybe Tyrion will ride a dragon himself.

00:57:14.160 --> 00:57:17.760
He does dream of riding a dragon and burning
his enemies.

00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:21.840
And author George Martin has hinted that Tyrion
will fly.

00:57:22.800 --> 00:57:27.280
Daenerys believes that her three dragons need
three riders.

00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:30.960
Jon Snow will probably ride one, like he does
in the TV show.

00:57:30.960 --> 00:57:35.920
He rides the green dragon, Rhaegal, who is
named after his [probable] father Rhaegar.

00:57:35.920 --> 00:57:38.800
Daenerys rides the black dragon, Drogon.

00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:44.720
So Tyrion could ride Viserion – Viserion
is coloured white and gold, and his blood

00:57:44.720 --> 00:57:49.360
is “gold and red” which fits Tyrion’s
Lannister colours.

00:57:49.360 --> 00:57:54.480
At the end of his latest preview chapter,
Tyrion dramatically picks up a white dragon

00:57:54.480 --> 00:58:00.000
cyvasse piece, which hints at a connection
between him and the white dragon Viserion.

00:58:00.720 --> 00:58:07.280
Usually, dragons are only ridden by Targaryens,
people with the Valyrian “blood of the dragon”.

00:58:07.280 --> 00:58:08.960
And Tyrion isn’t a Targaryen.

00:58:09.680 --> 00:58:10.400
Or is he?

00:58:11.280 --> 00:58:16.560
There is a theory that Tyrion is not the son
of Tywin Lannister, he’s actually the son

00:58:16.560 --> 00:58:19.040
of the Mad King, Aerys Targaryen.

00:58:19.600 --> 00:58:25.120
Cause for years, Aerys was sexually interested
in Tyrion’s mother, Joanna Lannister.

00:58:25.120 --> 00:58:30.080
It was rumoured that he took her virginity,
and that she was his mistress for a while.

00:58:30.080 --> 00:58:35.280
At Joanna’s wedding to Tywin, Aerys joked
that he wanted to have sex with her, and he

00:58:35.280 --> 00:58:37.360
took “liberties” at the bedding.

00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:43.840
Aerys’ wife complained that Aerys was turning
her ladies into his “whores”, so Joanna

00:58:43.840 --> 00:58:46.320
went back to Casterly Rock for a while.

00:58:46.320 --> 00:58:52.240
But then, the year before Tyrion was born,
Aerys and Joanna were both at a tournament

00:58:52.240 --> 00:58:53.520
in King’s Landing.

00:58:53.520 --> 00:58:59.040
Aerys made comments about Joanna’s breasts,
and Tywin got so angry that he tried to resign

00:58:59.040 --> 00:58:59.760
as Hand.

00:59:00.400 --> 00:59:02.960
The next year, Tyrion was born.

00:59:03.520 --> 00:59:08.640
So maybe, at this tournament, Aerys had sex
with Joanna and fathered Tyrion.

00:59:09.360 --> 00:59:14.480
Being a Targaryen could explain Tyrion’s
pale blond hair, which looks more like the

00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:18.720
Targaryen silvery blond than the Lannister
golden blond.

00:59:18.720 --> 00:59:23.680
Tyrion’s green eye could be from his Lannister
mother, and his black eye could actually be

00:59:23.680 --> 00:59:26.320
a very dark Targaryen purple.

00:59:26.320 --> 00:59:31.360
Targaryen blood could explain why Tyrion doesn’t
catch greyscale or the bloody flux – because

00:59:31.360 --> 00:59:33.200
Targaryens tend not to get sick.

00:59:33.760 --> 00:59:38.480
It could explain Tyrion’s dreams of dragons,
which are common in Targaryens.

00:59:38.480 --> 00:59:42.320
And Targaryen blood could let Tyrion ride
a dragon.

00:59:42.880 --> 00:59:46.560
In Book 5, Daenerys’ dragons like Ben Plumm.

00:59:46.560 --> 00:59:51.520
And Tyrion explains that this is because Ben
has some Targaryen blood in his family tree.

00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:55.760
Maybe the reason this is mentioned in the
book is so that when Tyrion meets Daenerys’

00:59:55.760 --> 01:00:01.600
dragons, they’ll like him too, hinting that
Tyrion also has Targaryen blood.

01:00:01.600 --> 01:00:07.120
And then Barristan, who was Aerys’ guard
for years, could reveal that Aerys is Tyrion’s

01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:08.000
father.

01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:14.240
It all fits – the white dragon, the timeline,
his appearance, his dreams – Tyrion could

01:00:14.240 --> 01:00:15.680
be a Targaryen.

01:00:16.400 --> 01:00:20.800
But does the story really need another secret
Targaryen?

01:00:20.800 --> 01:00:25.840
We’ve already got Jon Snow probably being
a secret Targaryen, and Young Griff being

01:00:25.840 --> 01:00:28.240
a secret Targaryen or a Blackfyre.

01:00:28.240 --> 01:00:30.880
Do we really need all three main characters&nbsp;

01:00:30.880 --> 01:00:34.000
to be Targaryens, whose&nbsp;
mothers died in childbirth,

01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:35.120
who ride dragons?

01:00:35.680 --> 01:00:40.640
And if Tyrion is Aerys’s son, what does
that mean for his relationship with Tywin?

01:00:40.640 --> 01:00:45.120
The whole point of their relationship is that
even though Tywin hates Tyrion, Tyrion is

01:00:45.120 --> 01:00:48.560
just like Tywin, Tyrion is Tywin “writ small”.

01:00:49.120 --> 01:00:52.400
Isn’t that ruined if Tyrion is actually
Aerys’ son?

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:58.400
You could argue that even if Aerys is Tyrion’s
biological father, Tywin is the father who

01:00:58.400 --> 01:01:02.880
raised Tyrion, and his shitty parenting made
Tyrion who he is.

01:01:03.440 --> 01:01:08.880
It’s like how even if Rhaegar is Jon Snow’s
biological father, Ned Stark is the father

01:01:08.880 --> 01:01:11.600
who raised Jon, and made him the person who
he is.

01:01:12.240 --> 01:01:17.840
And it kind of makes sense if Tywin always
suspected that Tyrion was Aerys’ son.

01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:23.280
Like, he does say that Tyrion is not his son,
but that he just cannot prove that Tyrion

01:01:23.280 --> 01:01:23.840
isn’t his.

01:01:24.560 --> 01:01:28.640
Cause there is no proof whether Tyrion is
a Targaryen.

01:01:28.640 --> 01:01:29.680
Only hints.

01:01:29.680 --> 01:01:33.040
And maybe that ambiguity is the point.

01:01:33.040 --> 01:01:35.440
Maybe we’ll never know for sure.

01:01:35.440 --> 01:01:40.240
Like, maybe Tyrion will start to develop a
connection with Viserion, but then Viserion

01:01:40.240 --> 01:01:45.440
will be killed or taken by Euron before Tyrion
can fully explore his Targaryen side.

01:01:45.440 --> 01:01:51.840
So maybe he’ll always question his identity
– is he a Lannister or a Targaryen?

01:01:51.840 --> 01:01:57.920
Tywin wondered the same thing – he was never
quite sure if Tyrion was his son, he didn’t

01:01:57.920 --> 01:02:00.560
want to believe Tyrion was his.

01:02:00.560 --> 01:02:06.000
Because Tyrion was a reflection of everything
Tywin hated about himself.

01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:11.760
It’s because Tyrion is so much like Tywin
that Tywin denied Tyrion was his, and preferred

01:02:11.760 --> 01:02:14.560
to believe he was Aerys’ instead.

01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:20.160
But Tyrion, unlike Tywin, could face the truth
– that it doesn’t matter whether Aerys

01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:22.000
is his biological father.

01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:28.000
Tyrion was raised as a Lannister, his personality
and values were shaped by Tywin, so for better

01:02:28.000 --> 01:02:32.560
or worse, no matter what’s in his blood,
“Tyrion is Tywin’s son”.

01:02:33.680 --> 01:02:38.400
And besides, George Martin has hinted that
the third dragonrider doesn’t necessarily

01:02:38.400 --> 01:02:42.480
need to be a Targaryen, so maybe Tyrion could
ride a dragon either way.

01:02:43.120 --> 01:02:48.320
The other thing Tyrion needs to resolve are
his feelings about Tysha – his pain and

01:02:48.320 --> 01:02:50.400
his longing for his lost love.

01:02:50.960 --> 01:02:54.000
Will he ever find “where whores go”?

01:02:54.000 --> 01:02:57.440
George Martin has said that we will find out
where whores go.

01:02:57.440 --> 01:02:58.800
So… where?

01:02:59.600 --> 01:03:03.840
In Braavos, Arya meets a sex worker called
the Sailor’s Wife.

01:03:03.840 --> 01:03:09.520
Before she has sex with men, she always marries
them in a fun temporary ceremony with a drunken

01:03:09.520 --> 01:03:15.680
priest – like how Tysha married Tyrion in
a fun ceremony with a drunken priest.

01:03:15.680 --> 01:03:20.480
The Sailor’s Wife likes singing, like how
Tysha used to sing for Tyrion.

01:03:20.480 --> 01:03:25.280
And she’s a “whore”, just like Tysha
was supposedly a “whore”.

01:03:25.280 --> 01:03:30.800
The Sailor’s Wife is a fun, and kind person,
though there’s something sad about her too.

01:03:31.360 --> 01:03:36.400
She often prays for her first husband, her
true love, to come back to her.

01:03:36.400 --> 01:03:41.440
Maybe that husband was Tyrion, and the Sailor’s
Wife is Tysha.

01:03:41.440 --> 01:03:45.360
She could’ve fled from Westeros, and set
herself up in Braavos.

01:03:45.360 --> 01:03:50.160
And thing is, the Sailor’s Wife has a blonde
daughter called Lanna.

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:56.400
Lanna is fourteen years old, and Tysha and
Tyrion were married either fourteen or fifteen

01:03:56.400 --> 01:03:57.120
years ago.

01:03:57.680 --> 01:04:03.600
So the timeline fits – Lanna could be Tyrion
Lannister’s daughter with Tysha.

01:04:04.320 --> 01:04:08.640
There are problems with this theory – like,
the Sailor’s Wife says her husband was..

01:04:08.640 --> 01:04:09.360
a sailor.

01:04:09.360 --> 01:04:14.160
And Tyrion’s not a sailor – so maybe her
husband was actually Tyrion’s uncle Gerion.

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:18.320
But the sailor thing could just be a lie she
tells to protect herself.

01:04:18.960 --> 01:04:22.480
The other problem is that a fortune-teller
says that the Sailor’s Wife’s husband

01:04:22.480 --> 01:04:26.800
is dead, and if he comes back to her, it will
be as a corpse.

01:04:27.440 --> 01:04:29.840
Tyrion isn’t literally dead.

01:04:29.840 --> 01:04:32.800
But he does think of himself&nbsp;
as being metaphorically&nbsp;

01:04:32.800 --> 01:04:35.280
dead, having died in King’s Landing and

01:04:35.280 --> 01:04:36.560
become a ghost.

01:04:37.280 --> 01:04:43.360
So if The Sailor’s Wife is Tysha, maybe
he will come back to her, in Braavos.

01:04:43.360 --> 01:04:48.240
Daenerys and Tyrion could stop there on the
way west – maybe Daenerys could borrow money

01:04:48.240 --> 01:04:51.520
from the Iron Bank, or fight the Faceless
Men or something.

01:04:51.520 --> 01:04:55.520
But Tyrion and Tysha’s reunion may not be
a happy one.

01:04:55.520 --> 01:05:00.480
Because Tyrion and Tysha aren’t the innocent
teenagers they remember each other as.

01:05:00.480 --> 01:05:07.200
Tyrion has become a “corpse” – a hateful
murderous version of the boy he used to be,

01:05:07.200 --> 01:05:12.800
and Tysha has.. ironically become a “whore”,
which is what Tyrion always feared she was.

01:05:13.520 --> 01:05:19.520
If a reunion with Tysha goes badly, and they
don’t meet each others’ impossible idealised

01:05:19.520 --> 01:05:26.080
standards, that could push Tyrion into an
even darker more destructive place – right

01:05:26.080 --> 01:05:28.640
as he arrives back at Westeros.

01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:35.440
So in the next book, Daenerys will carve a
bloody path across Essos, with Tyrion by her

01:05:35.440 --> 01:05:36.320
side.

01:05:36.320 --> 01:05:43.360
Tyrion might ride a dragon, he might reunite
with Tysha, and he might lose or kill Penny.

01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:51.760
Winds has the potential to be Tyrion’s darkest
book, where he fully embraces fire and blood.

01:05:52.640 --> 01:05:57.600
At the end of the TV show, Daenerys
burns King’s Landing, killing thousands

01:05:57.600 --> 01:06:01.360
of innocent people out of anger and frustration.

01:06:01.360 --> 01:06:06.800
And a lot of people complained that this terrible
dark turn happened too suddenly.

01:06:06.800 --> 01:06:11.920
There wasn’t enough buildup and exploration
of why Daenerys would do something so evil.

01:06:12.560 --> 01:06:17.840
In the books, her journey across Essos could
be that gradual buildup of destruction.

01:06:18.400 --> 01:06:24.080
Her allies and advisors in the books will
be violent fiery people like Tatters and Ben

01:06:24.080 --> 01:06:30.640
and Moqorro, the ironborn and Dothraki.. and
Tyrion, the devil on her shoulder, urging

01:06:30.640 --> 01:06:33.440
her to burn Westeros for his revenge.

01:06:34.160 --> 01:06:36.960
The situation in King’s Landing will be
different.

01:06:36.960 --> 01:06:42.480
It might be Aegon, not Cersei, who has the
Throne, possibly in alliance with Dorne, the

01:06:42.480 --> 01:06:43.840
Reach and the Faith.

01:06:43.840 --> 01:06:48.720
And Aegon may be popular with the common people
– there’s a vision of the mummer’s dragon

01:06:48.720 --> 01:06:50.960
“amidst a cheering crowd”.

01:06:50.960 --> 01:06:57.120
If the common people support Aegon over Daenerys,
Daenerys may see the people as her enemies.

01:06:57.680 --> 01:07:03.040
Jon Connington could be there, and interestingly,
JonCon has a traumatic backstory involving

01:07:03.040 --> 01:07:07.600
bells, which might be the reason for the bells
that ring in the show before Daenerys burns

01:07:07.600 --> 01:07:08.100
the city.

01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:11.040
There also could be wildfire in the mix.

01:07:11.040 --> 01:07:15.120
Cersei and Jaime might be there, perhaps as
prisoners of Aegon.

01:07:15.120 --> 01:07:18.240
And the spark behind the fire could be Tyrion.

01:07:18.880 --> 01:07:24.960
Cause King’s Landing is where Tyrion was
betrayed by Tywin, Cersei, Jaime, and Shae.

01:07:24.960 --> 01:07:30.160
It’s the city he fought to save before its
people rejected and condemned him.

01:07:30.160 --> 01:07:36.480
He said he wished he had enough poison to
kill them all, and ever since he’s wanted

01:07:36.480 --> 01:07:38.960
revenge, to pay his debts.

01:07:39.840 --> 01:07:45.440
During Robert’s Rebellion, Tywin brutally
sacked King’s Landing, killing men women

01:07:45.440 --> 01:07:46.400
and children.

01:07:46.400 --> 01:07:51.360
And part of the reason why he did this so
savagely was probably to get revenge on King

01:07:51.360 --> 01:07:54.400
Aerys and everyone else&nbsp;
who mocked and disrespected&nbsp;

01:07:54.400 --> 01:07:55.840
him when he was Hand of the King.

01:07:56.640 --> 01:08:02.160
Now Tyrion is set to repeat history, and to
attack that same city because of how he was

01:08:02.160 --> 01:08:04.400
treated when he was Hand of the King.

01:08:04.400 --> 01:08:07.760
Tyrion will repeat the sins of his father.

01:08:08.480 --> 01:08:12.880
In the show, Tyrion tells Daenerys not to
burn King’s Landing, but in the books, he

01:08:12.880 --> 01:08:18.400
could encourage or manipulate her into doing
it, by turning her against Aegon and the common

01:08:18.400 --> 01:08:25.040
people, or by not telling her about the dangerous
wildfire, or even by starting the fire on

01:08:25.040 --> 01:08:26.560
a dragon of his own.

01:08:26.560 --> 01:08:32.560
However it happens, the burning King’s Landing
would be the ultimate expression of Tyrion’s

01:08:32.560 --> 01:08:37.040
hate and pain, especially if it kills Jaime
and Cersei.

01:08:37.600 --> 01:08:41.680
But revenge won’t make Tyrion happy in the
end.

01:08:41.680 --> 01:08:46.400
In Book 5, he has a dream where he fights
a battle with dragons overhead.

01:08:46.400 --> 01:08:52.080
He kills Tywin, and he kills Jaime, but then
Tyrion realises he’s crying.

01:08:52.080 --> 01:08:55.600
As Ellaria says, revenge doesn’t fix anything.

01:08:55.600 --> 01:08:57.760
It doesn’t bring back what you’ve lost.

01:08:57.760 --> 01:08:59.920
A skull can’t make you happy.

01:09:00.560 --> 01:09:05.600
In the show, Tyrion walks through the ashes
of King’s Landing, and cries over the bodies

01:09:05.600 --> 01:09:07.360
of Jaime and Cersei.

01:09:07.360 --> 01:09:11.760
The tragedy in the show is that Tyrion failed
to protect his family.

01:09:11.760 --> 01:09:17.200
But in the books, the tragedy could be that
he killed his family, and only realised it

01:09:17.200 --> 01:09:19.840
was a mistake when it was too late.

01:09:20.400 --> 01:09:25.840
In the show, Bran makes Tyrion Hand of the
King, and says he’ll work to fix his “terrible

01:09:25.840 --> 01:09:26.880
mistakes”.

01:09:26.880 --> 01:09:32.960
But Tyrion’s terrible mistake in the TV
show was believing in Daenerys, who turned

01:09:32.960 --> 01:09:35.920
evil despite his good intentions.

01:09:35.920 --> 01:09:40.480
It could be so much more tragic in the books
if Tyrion’s “mistake” is encouraging

01:09:40.480 --> 01:09:44.320
Daenerys’ violence, choosing hate and revenge.

01:09:45.200 --> 01:09:50.080
So will Tyrion end the series as a villain,
like Tywin?

01:09:50.080 --> 01:09:52.160
Or could he redeem himself?

01:09:52.960 --> 01:09:56.880
In the show, the white walkers are defeated,
then King’s Landing burns.

01:09:56.880 --> 01:10:01.280
But in the books, it might be the other way
around – because Jon killing Daenerys makes

01:10:01.280 --> 01:10:05.920
more sense in the context of the white walkers,
because of the Azor Ahai story – so maybe

01:10:05.920 --> 01:10:11.200
after Tyrion and Daenerys burn King’s Landing,
Tyrion will help defeat the white walkers.

01:10:11.200 --> 01:10:17.280
He could finally realise that saving the world
is more important than politics and revenge.

01:10:17.280 --> 01:10:21.920
The Night’s Watch were right, this is what
he should have been doing all along.

01:10:21.920 --> 01:10:27.680
When Tyrion stood on the Wall in Book 1, he
felt something, he sensed that the white walkers

01:10:27.680 --> 01:10:29.440
were the true enemy.

01:10:29.440 --> 01:10:34.480
He could help fight them by riding a dragon
maybe, or just help politically, by building

01:10:34.480 --> 01:10:36.400
alliances with the Starks.

01:10:36.400 --> 01:10:41.120
Tyrion and Jon still think of each other as
friends, and Tyrion has relationships with

01:10:41.120 --> 01:10:43.680
Bran and his wife Sansa.

01:10:43.680 --> 01:10:48.800
So maybe Tyrion will team up with the Starks
and redeem himself by saving the world from

01:10:48.800 --> 01:10:49.680
the white walkers.

01:10:50.400 --> 01:10:53.680
Or maybe that’s too much of a happy ending.

01:10:53.680 --> 01:10:56.400
Maybe Tyrion deserves punishment.

01:10:57.200 --> 01:11:02.800
Characters talk about cutting out Tyrion’s
tongue eight times in the books.

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:08.080
Because Tyrion constantly annoys people with
his jokes and insults, and his words cause

01:11:08.080 --> 01:11:09.600
so much trouble.

01:11:09.600 --> 01:11:13.360
Removing someone’s tongue is a common punishment
in Westeros.

01:11:13.360 --> 01:11:18.000
Euron Greyjoy often cuts out peoples’ tongues,
and he’s becoming a major bad guy in the

01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:18.560
books.

01:11:18.560 --> 01:11:23.600
He might take Tyrion’s dragon Viserion,
before taking Tyrion’s tongue.

01:11:24.240 --> 01:11:29.440
Cersei is another possibility – she hates
Tyrion, and she’s been talking a lot about

01:11:29.440 --> 01:11:30.720
cutting out tongues lately.

01:11:31.440 --> 01:11:36.320
Tyrion losing his tongue would fit a pattern
with his siblings – cause each of the Lannisters

01:11:36.320 --> 01:11:40.160
lose the part of themselves that give them
power and pride.

01:11:40.160 --> 01:11:43.840
Jaime loses his hand that made him a great
warrior.

01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:48.800
Cersei loses her image as a proud beautiful
queen in her walk of shame.

01:11:48.800 --> 01:11:54.480
And Tyrion’s power and pride is in his sharp
witty tongue, so if he loses his tongue, all

01:11:54.480 --> 01:11:57.600
three Lannisters will have lost their most
important part.

01:11:58.320 --> 01:12:03.280
When Jaime loses his hand, and Bran breaks
his back, and Arya loses her sight, these

01:12:03.280 --> 01:12:08.160
are challenges that force the characters to
grow and redefine themselves.

01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:13.600
But Tyrion has kind of already had his downfall
– he’s already lost everything.

01:12:13.600 --> 01:12:17.760
So losing his tongue might not be about growing
his character.

01:12:17.760 --> 01:12:23.760
It could be more of a brutal final tragedy
at the end of his story, as a punishment for

01:12:23.760 --> 01:12:24.960
all his crimes.

01:12:25.760 --> 01:12:31.440
If Tyrion’s words and lies convince Daenerys
to burn King’s Landing, maybe King Bran

01:12:31.440 --> 01:12:36.160
will take Tyrion’s tongue so his words can’t
do evil again.

01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:41.680
He could live out his days as a quiet lion
at Casterly Rock, or as a mute maester at

01:12:41.680 --> 01:12:45.040
the Citadel, or with the Night’s Watch.

01:12:45.040 --> 01:12:50.240
Tyrion remembers that Jeor Mormont said they
need men like Tyrion in the Watch.

01:12:50.240 --> 01:12:55.918
Tyrion remembers that the Watch welcomes outcasts
and misfits no matter their past crimes – which

01:12:55.918 --> 01:12:56.320
is perfect for a criminal outcast like Tyrion.

01:12:56.320 --> 01:13:01.680
Maybe with the brotherhood of the Watch, Tyrion
will finally find the family and acceptance

01:13:01.680 --> 01:13:03.200
he’s always wanted.

01:13:03.200 --> 01:13:07.680
Sam says that someone really needs to sort
through the books in the Castle Black library,

01:13:07.680 --> 01:13:09.920
which’ll take years of work.

01:13:09.920 --> 01:13:12.160
But Sam will be busy being Grand Maester.

01:13:12.160 --> 01:13:15.520
So maybe Tyrion could sort out the Night’s
Watch’s books.

01:13:15.520 --> 01:13:21.280
Tyrion’s first chapter begins with him reading
a book – that was always his comfort and

01:13:21.280 --> 01:13:22.400
his escape.

01:13:22.400 --> 01:13:27.360
So maybe the series will end with Tyrion reading
a book – quietly.

01:13:28.880 --> 01:13:31.840
So is Tyrion Lannister a villain?

01:13:31.840 --> 01:13:35.440
From the beginning, Tyrion felt unloved and
rejected.

01:13:35.440 --> 01:13:39.040
So he used political power to try to earn
some respect.

01:13:39.040 --> 01:13:43.760
But then he was betrayed and condemned by
the people closest to him.

01:13:43.760 --> 01:13:49.200
So Tyrion falls deep into despair and hate,
and dreams of revenge.

01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:52.880
In the next book, he may embrace fire and
blood.

01:13:52.880 --> 01:13:55.520
He might spark the burning of King’s Landing.

01:13:55.520 --> 01:13:59.120
But he might also help save the world from
the white walkers.

01:13:59.120 --> 01:14:05.680
Tyrion is villainous – he’s a hateful,
ruthless murderer, like his father.

01:14:05.680 --> 01:14:11.200
But he is also heroic – he is sometimes
kind, protective and brave.

01:14:11.920 --> 01:14:17.680
George Martin did once call Tyrion a villain,
but he more often calls Tyrion morally grey.

01:14:18.240 --> 01:14:21.920
Martin writes about the human heart in conflict
with itself.

01:14:21.920 --> 01:14:25.440
And no one’s heart is more conflicted than
Tyrion’s.

01:14:26.000 --> 01:14:30.240
There’s love and hate, good and evil inside
him.

01:14:30.240 --> 01:14:32.960
And to be human is to look for the light.

01:14:34.560 --> 01:14:38.880
If you want the real story of Game of Thrones,
you’ve got to check out the books – the

01:14:38.880 --> 01:14:42.480
main series, and the prequel stories, and
the history books.

01:14:42.480 --> 01:14:46.880
You can get any one of these on audiobook
for free right now, at audible.com/asx.

